Priority: 2
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-tablet-pressure-and-stroke-width

Goal:
Make stroke rendering scale visually with zoom so thin strokes stay thin when zoomed out and get proportionally larger when zoomed in.

Context:
The user reported that stroke width currently appears too constant across zoom levels, which makes thin marks look bloated when zoomed far out.

Expected changes:

- audit current stroke-width math during canvas rendering
- make stroke appearance respond correctly to camera zoom
- verify the behavior for freehand strokes and shape outlines where the same width logic applies

Acceptance criteria:

- Zooming out makes thin strokes appear proportionally thinner on screen.
- Zooming in makes strokes appear proportionally larger on screen.
- Stroke rendering does not jump, explode, or become unreadable at normal zoom ranges.

Notes:

- Keep this scoped to viewport rendering behavior first; do not widen into pressure-model redesign.

